==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*na}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{ru-IPA|на́-}} {{i|when stressed}}

===Prefix===
{{head|ru|prefix|cat2=verbal prefixes}}

# {{lb|ru|used with verbs}} [[onto]], [[upon]]
#: {{prefex|ru|идти́|t1=to go|найти́|t2=to find|lit2=to come upon}}
# {{lb|ru|used with verbs}} to [[repletion]], to [[satiation]], [[to the full]], [[enough]], [[too much]]
#: {{prefex|ru|пить|t1=to drink|-ся|pos2=reflexive suffix|напи́ться|t3=to drink to the full; to quench one’s thirst; to get drunk}}
# {{lb|ru|used with verbs}} a [[quantity]] of, a [[lot]] of
#: {{prefex|ru|купи́ть|t1=to buy|[[накупи́ть]] [[книга|книг]]|t2=to buy a quantity of books, a lot of books}}

====Usage notes====
* The stressed variant is found in the following situations:
*# the past participle of verbs with a one-syllable root ending in {{lang|ru|-ать}}: e.g. {{m|ru|на́званный}} from {{m|ru|назва́ть}}, {{m|ru|на́чатый}} from {{m|ru|нача́ть}};
*# some deverbal nouns: e.g. {{m|ru|на́тиск||[[onslaught]], [[pressure]]}} from {{m|ru|нати́скать}};
*# some adverbs: e.g. {{m|ru|на́прочь||[[absolutely]], [[without]] a [[trace]] {{i|colloquial}}}}, {{m|ru|на́смерть||to [[death]], [[utterly]]}}, {{m|ru|на́земь||[[down]], [[onto]] the [[ground]] {{i|poetic}}}}.

